<Base title="About" description="About Chris Cerne and stalactech.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="posttitle">About</h1>
    <article>
      <p>I'm Chris Cerne. stalactech is where I publish research as I do it: language-model experiments, getting Graal / GS2 to run on a Nintendo Switch, decompiler internals, and vulnerability write-ups. The point is sharing discoveries with the research community, not a pitch.</p>
      <p>By day I'm a <strong>Security Engineer at Meta</strong> (at Meta since November 2025; in this role since June 2026). Before that: Senior Security Consultant at Stratum Security (August 2023–2025), and Security Consultant at Bishop Fox (January 2022–August 2023).</p>
      <p>Independent vulnerability research includes credited CVEs CVE-2020-8797, CVE-2020-8798, and CVE-2020-12123 through CVE-2020-12127, plus participation in the Synack Red Team and Google's Vulnerability Reward Program. Bug reports and disclosures live under <a href="/tags/vulnerability-research">vulnerability research</a>.</p>
      <p>Education: Virginia Tech, B.S. Computer Science, 2021.</p>
      <p>Find me on <a href="https://github.com/cernec1999">GitHub</a>, or follow the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>. Recruiters: my <a href="/resume">resume is here</a>, with a <a href="/resume.pdf">PDF version</a> if you need one.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
